                                "sense_id": "95cafc5f-a683-3d37-bf18-900fd81a7345",
                                "text": "René Decartes ist ein klassischer Vertreter des Rationalismus."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "985f9280-9477-4676-9eb9-7cf9e2721c32",
                        "source_entry_id": "f5d4e8d9-8376-3c99-8a80-9091ffb801c6",
                        "source_sense_id": "95cafc5f-a683-3d37-bf18-900fd81a7345",
                        "target_lang_word": "理性主义",
                        "target_lang_code": "zh",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "61188a67-3d36-4678-82af-c1059a27cb4d",
                        "source_entry_id": "f5d4e8d9-8376-3c99-8a80-9091ffb801c6",
                        "source_sense_id": "95cafc5f-a683-3d37-bf18-900fd81a7345",
                        "target_lang_word": "rationalism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rationalism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7813435e-0417-30e5-a628-af6b49a0ac03",
                                        "entry_id": "16fb52fc-2fd6-3218-a92f-a601a39af6a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The theory that the reason is a source of knowledge independent of and superior to sense perception."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "635ac29b-c28f-3986-8ebb-04aee7886d68",
                                        "entry_id": "16fb52fc-2fd6-3218-a92f-a601a39af6a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The theory that knowledge may be derived by deductions from a priori concepts (such as axioms, postulates or earlier deductions)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b8d5bdc-0f01-3412-8431-0c2ccc66e537",
                                        "entry_id": "16fb52fc-2fd6-3218-a92f-a601a39af6a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A view that the fundamental method for problem solving is through reason and experience rather than faith, inspiration, revelation, intuition or authority."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f4ada588-8fd9-4113-b321-251848401255",
                                                "sense_id": "0b8d5bdc-0f01-3412-8431-0c2ccc66e537",
                                                "text": "The opinion opposed to mysticism in philosophy is sometimes spoken of as rationalism. Rationalism insists that all our beliefs ought ultimately to find for themselves articulate grounds. Such grounds, for rationalism, must consist of four things: (1) definitely statable abstract principles; (2) definite facts of sensation; (3) definite hypotheses based on such facts; and (4) definite inferences logically drawn."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "10169985-0167-39a6-941a-1710cff993dc",
                                        "entry_id": "16fb52fc-2fd6-3218-a92f-a601a39af6a5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Elaboration of theories by use of reason alone without appeal to experience, such as in mathematical systems."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ca8353ae-add6-49f8-9c8a-553ef64b62a8",
                        "source_entry_id": "f5d4e8d9-8376-3c99-8a80-9091ffb801c6",
                        "source_sense_id": "95cafc5f-a683-3d37-bf18-900fd81a7345",
                        "target_lang_word": "rationalisme",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rationalisme",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0822fb8a-cab3-3c8d-8bf0-8e1038560c98",
                                        "entry_id": "ac0d76cd-4326-3a81-bad3-c43db2e70a05",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Doctrine qui pose la raison comme seule source de connaissance."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57d90417-5fa3-4290-bbd8-8d89f3a1136f",
                                                "sense_id": "0822fb8a-cab3-3c8d-8bf0-8e1038560c98",
                                                "text": "Le triomphe du rationalisme ne fut pas aussi grand, mais il le fut autant qu’il pouvait l’être. Descartes eut le bonheur de rencontrer deux adversaires puissants, Gassendi et Hobbes, l’un le plus érudit et le plus habile, l’autre le plus radical et le plus conséquent des sensualistes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebe99574-fc0b-4937-bcc1-84a6d82c1c67",
                                                "sense_id": "0822fb8a-cab3-3c8d-8bf0-8e1038560c98",
                                                "text": "Le rationalisme des Dialecticiens n’était pas sans faire courir un grave danger à la foi."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08f69e0a-cdcb-4e56-8660-a9fb593baee8",
                                                "sense_id": "0822fb8a-cab3-3c8d-8bf0-8e1038560c98",
                                                "text": "Au cœur de l’islam, la bataille fit rage quelque temps entre ceux qu’attirait le rationalisme grec d’un côté et, de l’autre, ceux qui mettaient l’accent sur la prééminence de la Parole révélée de Dieu comme seule explication des phénomènes humains et naturels."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "07a3ce8c-d303-3abc-888a-1f2059d0cec5",
                                        "entry_id": "ac0d76cd-4326-3a81-bad3-c43db2e70a05",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Toute doctrine qui considère les choses uniquement d’après les données de la raison."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
